Z||000000||Xtreme Fiero's||09-27-2000||11:39 PM||||<BR>I got a post card today from RYANE Motorspors at said they will NOT sell Fiero/Kit car parts after September 30th 2000. And that any party that would like to take over production of thier Fiero/ Kit car products to contact Daryl Armstrong.<P>What the hell happend? RYANE kicks ass!!!! (used to)||||reg||11
Z||000001||Wannabe||09-28-2000||06:44 PM||||It really is remarkable to see how little interest there seems to be in the passing of one of the biggest supporters of the Fiero aftemarket. With the effort and expense it takes to develop and bring special products like those offered by Ryane to the market, it is really a wonder that they ever went to the trouble, or that any other vendors do. As Fiero enthusiasts, we should count ourselves as lucky that some vendors shows this kind of commitment to the Fiero marketplace, especially when there is so much money to be made from the import market. Nobody is likely to get rich selling Fiero parts. If we want to continue to have these kinds of products and services available to us, we need to support and encourage vendors as much as possible, and keep in mind that with limited production volumes, there are bound to be some glitches. <P>I really disapointed that Ryane has chosen to get out of the Fiero business, especially since the plan was to outfit my '87GT with pretty much their full line of equipment. Too bad  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||09-28-2000||06:44 PM||||thier making Civic, integra and DSM stuff now!!! we have some of their stuff at the shop! super nice!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||09-28-2000||09:38 PM||||Is it as expensive as the Fiero stuff?<BR>It seems like their parts are higher than similar parts from other manufacturers.<BR>(I may be wrong. That multi-thousand dollar suspension kit keeps coming to mind, though.)<BR>I know that my pockets are not deep enough to afford most of their products. Perhaps others feel the same? <BR>Just my $.02.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (soon to receive transplant.)<BR>88 "pretzeled" Formula <P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wannabe||09-28-2000||10:41 PM||||Someone I know bought all there suspension pieces from various suppliers...bushings here, a sway bar and springs there and shocks somewhere else. By the time they were done, they could have purchased the complete Rayne suspension with coil overs in front for just a few hundred dollars more. At $900 for the front suspension kit, that's a deal. The more expensive "Slalom" kit, well, that's obviously not for everyone.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Lunapark||09-29-2000||04:37 AM||||I know Daryl and have know him for years. I purchased the entire Suspension, Crossmember brakes setup from him.  Once I received the stuff from him it was great. The problem was that it took 8 months to get it. Yea its great to have all these companies support the car, but if they can't deliver in a timely manner, what good is it. And to be quite honest, being that I have 3 Fieros and I have the RCC stuff on another Fiero and the 88 GT suspension from Pontiac on the last one it being the pontiac suspension rides and handles a whole lot better than either one of these setups. <BR>Neither one of the $5000.00 Ryane or the $3000 RCC was worth the trouble. I still enjoy the Factory 88 setup better. <BR>Sorry.<BR>For all you people who will miss Ryane KONI will make you a custom set of coil overs for your Fiero, front and Rear for $1100.00. <BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||6
